 # MLPRender_Fea
 
-Also called: MLP Render, MLP Render with Feature Encoding, MLP Render with Feature and View Positional Encoding, MLP Render with Features, MLP for volume rendering, Neural Radiance Fields network
+Also called: Color MLP pipeline, Color Prediction Pipeline, MLP Render, MLP Render with Feature Encoding, MLP Render with Feature and View Positional Encoding, MLP Render with Features, MLP for volume rendering, Neural Radiance Fields network
 
 ## Overview
-MLPRender_Fea is a neural rendering module that predicts RGB color from input features, view directions, and positions using a Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) with positional encoding applied to features and view direction, but NOT position [S6, unofficial]. It solves the problem of view-dependent appearance synthesis by mapping high-dimensional input vectors to a 3D color space [S1]. It sets itself apart from its parent [NeRF MLP Architecture](910-nerf-mlp-architecture.md) by explicitly separating the positional information (handled by the feature grid or upstream encoder) from the appearance decoding, applying positional encoding only to features and view directions [S6, unofficial]. Unlike [NeRF with Per-Image Embeddings](2484-nerf-with-per-image-embeddings.md) which injects global image context, or [Linear Feature Decoder with Learned Color Basis](3352-linear-feature-decoder-with-learned-color-basis.md) which uses linear projections, this method explicitly encodes view directions to model view-dependent appearance [S1].
+MLPRender_Fea is a neural rendering module that predicts RGB color from input features, view directions, and optional positional encodings using a Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) [S3, S7, unofficial]. It solves the problem of mapping continuous spatial features to view-dependent radiance values in neural implicit representations [S7, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from its parent [NeRF MLP Architecture](910-nerf-mlp-architecture.md) by explicitly decoupling the input representation: it accepts pre-computed features (e.g., from a voxel grid, triplanes, or other encoders) and view directions as inputs, rather than raw 3D coordinates and viewing directions [S7, unofficial]. Unlike [NeRF with Per-Image Embeddings](2484-nerf-with-per-image-embeddings.md) which injects global scene context, MLPRender_Fea processes local features directly [S7, unofficial].
 
